                <pb facs="0234" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.75/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Aldridge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-04T20:00:00+02:00">June 4, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 4—4 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>48. My 45, June 3, 11 p.m. Mr. Venizelos has overruled decision of Minister of
                    Communications and has informed me a few minutes ago through his private
                    secretary that telephone adjudication will be postponed until June 19. Mr. Gill
                    will therefore have time to reach Athens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldridge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
